---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
const piSource =
  "https://github.com/raspberrypi/documentation/tree/master/documentation/asciidoc/microcontrollers/pico-series/images";
const componentsSource = "https://github.com/raspberrypilearning/components";
---

<Site title="Image credits">
  <section class="wrap page-intro narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">PICTURES TO LEARN WITH</p>
    <h1>Image credits</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      The hardware pictures come from the people who make and document these
      parts.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section narrow prose">
    <h2>Raspberry Pi boards</h2>
    <p>
      Raspberry Pi Pico family photographs © Raspberry Pi, from the{" "}
      <a href={piSource}>
        official documentation’s pico-1s.png and pico-2s.png
      </a>
      . Used under{" "}
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>
      , as specified in the{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/raspberrypi/documentation/blob/master/LICENSE.md">
        documentation licence
      </a>
      . The pages show selected boards from the family photographs at different
      display sizes. Those selected views remain under the same licence.
    </p>
    <h2>Seeed Studio XIAO boards</h2>
    <p>
      Board photographs © Seeed Studio, from its{" "}
      <a href="https://wiki.seeedstudio.com/XIAO_ESP32C3_Getting_Started/">
        XIAO ESP32-C3
      </a>
      ,{" "}
      <a href="https://wiki.seeedstudio.com/xiao_esp32s3_getting_started/">
        XIAO ESP32-S3
      </a>{" "}
      and{" "}
      <a href="https://wiki.seeedstudio.com/xiao_esp32c6_getting_started/">
        XIAO ESP32-C6
      </a>{" "}
      guides. Used under{" "}
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>
      , under the{" "}
      <a href="https://wiki.seeedstudio.com/License/">
        Seeed documentation and images licence
      </a>
      . Images are unchanged apart from display size.
    </p>
    <h2>Component pictures</h2>
    <p>
      Addressable pixel, breadboard, jumper wires, 330 Ω resistor and capacitor
      images from{" "}
      <a href={componentsSource}>Components by the Raspberry Pi Foundation</a>,
      used under{" "}
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>.
      Source files are <code>adafruit-neopixel.png</code>,{" "}
      <code>breadboard.png</code>, <code>jumper-male-to-male.png</code>,{" "}
      <code>resistor-330r.png</code> and <code>capacitor.png</code>. Images are
      unchanged apart from display size. The capacitor picture illustrates the
      type of part; the build guide specifies the required rating.
    </p>
    <h2>Wiring diagrams</h2>
    <p>
      The quick and upgraded connection diagrams are drawn for KajLights, using
      the Pico pin documentation and{" "}
      <a href="https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-neopixel-uberguide/best-practices">
        Adafruit’s NeoPixel wiring guidance
      </a>{" "}
      and{" "}
      <a href="https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-neopixel-uberguide/logic-level">
        discussion of direct drive
      </a>{" "}
      as technical references. They show functional connections, not physical
      breadboard layouts. The quick route reflects Kaj’s experience driving
      strips directly from Picos; the later circuit adds a data resistor and
      level shifter.
    </p>
  </section>
</Site>
